\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Vector
\f1\b0 : When Sarah transmits the virus sexually, the virus interacts with specific enzymes and unique microflora within the reproductive tract.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Phenotypic Shift
\f1\b0 : This chemical environment causes the virus to undergo a structural, chimeric mutation. It morphs into a highly stable, slow-burning variant that completely lacks the corporate "two-week DRM off-switch."\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Six-Month Shield
\f1\b0 : This mutated variant infects a small cluster of reproductive stem cells, turning them into a tiny, permanent "micro-factory" that secretes Tardigrade Dsup and rejuvenation proteins into the bloodstream.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Phenotypic Tail
\f1\b0 : The active tissue rejuvenation takes around six months to naturally degrade back to the partner's baseline aging trajectory once the local micro-factory eventually winds down.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The TMinus Shield
\f1\b0 : For those six months, the circulating Tardigrade Dsup proteins bind to the partner's chromatin, creating a physical blanket over their DNA. This accidentally renders the partner completely immune to the airborne/waterborne TMinus deployment, as the TMinus integrase cannot access or scan the blanketed genome.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa265\partightenfactor0

